WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.101
-My next guest has

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.969
one of the biggest social media
followings in the world.

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.773
She's also the host of "A Little
Late with Lilly Singh."

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:09.241
Season 2 premiered last night

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:12.845
and airs weeknights
at 1:35 a.m. on NBC.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.447
Set your DVRs.

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.149
Here's our pal Lilly Singh.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.151
Oh!
-Hey, Jimmy, my man!

00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:20.252
So good to see you.
-Look at you.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.454
You look fantastic.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.889
Thank you so much for doing this
and being here.

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.024
-I know, I bring
all the Tinky-Winky vibes.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.459
-You do? [ Laughs ]

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.628
Is that Tinky-Winky?
I love that.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.696
-Boop.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.264
-Dude, last time
you were on the show --

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.032
By the way, congrats
on the show, Season 2.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.967
Watched last night.
-Thank you.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:36.870
-Loved your Kamala Harris.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.903
-Thank you.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.139
-And you had
a good little inside joke

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.941
about being on at 1:35.
I loved it.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.111
But the -- I was thinking,
I go, didn't --

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:48.714
'Cause I remember --
Somehow I connected you two

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:51.584
for some reason. I go,
"Why did I connect this?"

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:55.788
And you met President -- Vice
President-Elect Kamala Harris

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.257
on our show,
the last time you did our show.

00:00:58.257 --> 00:00:59.759
-Yes, I did.
And you don't understand

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.227
it's the biggest flex --
There it is.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.695
It's the biggest flex ever.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.496
I vividly remember.
I think this was actually

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:07.000
the day that was before
my Season 1 premiere.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.334
-Yes.
-Where, you know,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.103
Kamala Harris was
the first guest, and she came,

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.338
and they said, "Hey, Kamala
Harris would like to say hi."

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.607
And I was like,
"Uh, yes, absolutely."

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.677
And she proceeded
to just be amazing.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:21.047
She was like, "Lilly,
everything you're doing,

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:24.184
I love that you're doing it,
and it's so important.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:26.385
And you're a big voice
for the community."

00:01:26.385 --> 00:01:27.654
And she was saying
all these things

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:29.622
about how I'm so inspiring
and I'm paving a path.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.291
And I'm like,
you're Kamala Harris.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.893
Like, how are you
saying this to me?

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.228
-You're that. You're that.

00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.930
-I'm like, "Am I
in the Matrix right now?

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.532
Like, this is you.
You are that person."

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.934
-Who is talking about who? Yeah.
That's so funny.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:44.871
-You know that meme of
Spider-Man looking at himself?

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.773
-Yes, of course.
Dude, Spider-Man.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.242
-Literally, I was like,
"I am shook

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:51.277
that you're saying this about me
because --" And I have to say

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.913
that her energy and presence
was just so invigorating.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.915
I think I went out and did
my most comfortable performance

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.151
with you, Jimmy,
'cause I was Kamalafied.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.086
She Kamalafied me.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.455
-Kamalafied.
You became Kamalafied.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.822
And so you just came out
and just --

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:05.758
Yeah, you did rip it up
that night. It was great.

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.792
-Thank you.

00:02:06.792 --> 00:02:09.295
-I wanted to ask you
about what you --

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.332
'Cause quarantine, everyone's at
home and trying to be safe.

00:02:13.332 --> 00:02:16.803
But I think -- I did.
A lot of people did --

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.339
Took to social media
to just start doing things.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.708
And you, who I first
were introduced to you

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:26.746
because you were
a YouTube superstar,

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:30.550
uh, and I was going to ask you,
what did you think of all of it,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.018
and what did you think
of everyone's stuff?

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.921
-Yeah. I mean, you know,
like most people,

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.256
quarantine for me has been
a time of reflecting.

00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:40.292
It took a global pandemic
for me to sit and be like,

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:42.161
"What is my life?
What do I like?

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.863
What are my priorities?"

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.665
Um, and, you know,
I think I'm a big believer

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.233
that everything
is a double-edged sword. Right?

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.501
I love social media.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.969
I have a career
because of social media.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.005
I'm sitting here with you right
now because of social media.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.606
And so I do think
it's a wonderful tool

00:02:54.606 --> 00:02:56.408
to connect people,
to get informed,

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:58.077
to feel part of something.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.578
But, you know, I'd be remiss

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:02.381
if I didn't say
that it also can be quite toxic.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:06.052
And I think I got into
a little bit of a phase

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.354
where I thought
Twitter was real life

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.555
and Instagram was real life.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.258
And I was living in that world.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.427
And then I had to be like, "This
is not how I want to live."

00:03:15.427 --> 00:03:17.363
Like, there is so much
toxicity online.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.131
Um, and I talked about this
in the season --

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:20.433
in the premiere monologue,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:23.102
that especially during
the Black Lives Matter movement,

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.538
I felt like social media
was just so full of division.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.539
And I actually went to a protest
in real life,

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:28.674
and it was beautiful.

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:31.543
And for me, that was that moment
where I thought,

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:34.147
"The real world
deserves our attention,

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:36.682
as much or more than
I'm giving it on the phone."

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:40.420
And so I deleted social media
off my phone during quarantine.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.521
And it's been really great.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.022
I feel like
I'm a lot more present.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.190
-Really?

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.325
-Apparently,
there's trees outside.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:48.327
-No, no, that's not true.
-Don't know when that happened.

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:50.096
-There's trees in my backyard.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.231
I was like,
"When did these get here?"

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:55.468
-Wait, dude,
trees are trending right now.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:59.672
Trees are trending #2,
people rediscovering trees.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.473
They love it.
-Yeah, literally.

00:04:01.473 --> 00:04:03.609
-Yeah. That's so --

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:06.412
Wait, so you just
went no Twitter?

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.313
-Yeah, I mean,
I deleted it off my phone.

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:10.883
I won't lie. It's kind of like
a drunk relationship.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.685
Like you know how when people
get drunk, they text their ex?

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.620
My thing is if I get drunk,
I download Twitter.

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.589
Like, this is my relationship
with Twitter.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.690
I be drunk and I'm like,

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.758
"You know, just one tweet,

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:21.594
one quick -- It means nothing."

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.862
And then I download Twitter.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.831
So I definitely relapse
and have moments.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.734
But I try to not -- You know
what I'm trying to avoid, Jimmy?

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.904
I'm trying to avoid
the human tendency we have,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.874
where if we have a spare
four minutes before anything,

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.142
we go like this.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.277
-Yes.
-I'm trying to get rid of that.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.179
-Yeah.
-Because I'd rather do this.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.014
I'd rather be, like,
checking in with myself.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:45.852
I'd rather control the energy
I'm getting in my day.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.619
And I just don't want
to give that control away.

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:49.955
-Yeah, I find that, I go,

00:04:49.955 --> 00:04:52.158
"Oh, that is so annoying
if somebody does that."

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.726
And then once someone does it,

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:54.994
it makes me want
to look at my phone.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.495
-Exactly. Exactly.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.631
-What am I missing out on?
You know, and it's like --

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.932
-Because you
feel like the idiot.

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.568
You're like, "Oh,
should I be doing this, too?"

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.904
-Yeah. We have to find out
what's new, who's trending,

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.840
who hates who, what's going on.
It's like, "No, I --"

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:14.046
-And I find myself magnetically
attracted to comments and drama.

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.716
And that's on me.
I feel like I go onto anything,

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:18.017
I'm diving in the comments.

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.484
-It's human.
-"Oh, someone wrote something?

00:05:19.484 --> 00:05:23.122
What did people reply saying?"
And now I'm in this world

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.256
where I'm like,
"How did I get here?

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:25.557
Why do I care
about any of this?"

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.527
-Yeah, no,
it's just a human thing.

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:31.464
I wanted to ask you
about Season 2.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.232
You changed it up. It's great.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.333
-Thanks!

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:35.835
-I love that you did that.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.503
I think it's good.
You have to try --

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:40.206
Everyone should try new things
and see what sticks.

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:41.974
And it's like,
you totally changed it

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.976
from the first season.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.979
-I did. I grabbed it
by the reins, to be honest.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.181
You know, Season 1, for me --
I'll just be honest.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:50.782
I came on your show,
Jimmy, Season 1.

00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:53.119
I was wearing that green outfit,
and I came, and I said,

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:55.054
"I'm breaking the rules
of late night.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.423
You know, I'm going
to change the format."

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.292
And then I literally proceeded
to do the exact same format

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.562
and did everything that I said
I'm wasn't going to do.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.163
And I take that "L"
on my shoulders

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:07.934
because I think Season 1, I was
learning a complete new world.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.836
You know? The learning curve
was so steep for me.

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:14.606
And so, I found myself
not being completely myself.

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:16.475
I found myself
trying to be someone

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.177
that would please
the late-night world

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.911
and please all the articles
and headlines.

00:06:19.911 --> 00:06:22.748
And so I had to, like,
really have a talk with myself

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:26.552
before Season 2 and say,
"You need to make this you."

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.920
And that's what I've done.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.123
-Since you started the new
season, started last night,

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.658
but everyone should watch.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:35.727
After me, after Seth,
comes Lilly.

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:38.064
Uh, and so, 1:35, check it out.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:41.166
I want to ask you maybe
some new questions about you.

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:42.835
-Sure.
-Ready?

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.503
Alright. What is your new jam?

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.706
What's a new song
that you discovered?

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:48.707
-Hmm, okay, well,
Saweetie was my first guest,

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:51.443
and I discovered her song
"Best Friend" with Doja Cat.

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:56.181
And I can't twerk, but that song
makes me want to try.

00:06:56.181 --> 00:06:58.884
You know? It really makes me
want to try to twerk,

00:06:58.884 --> 00:06:59.985
and I love it.

00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:02.354
-What's a new game
that you've played?

00:07:02.354 --> 00:07:04.389
-Okay, so, I think
I'm late to the party here,

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:06.291
'cause I think people
have been on this for a while,

00:07:06.291 --> 00:07:08.828
but during the pandemic,
I discovered Catan.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:11.297
And now I am
a full-fledged nerd.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.532
And I play online and in-person,

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:16.602
and I am just --
Catan is my thing.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.037
-Dude, I want to make a T-shirt

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:20.673
that says,
"Nobody wants your sheep."

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.276
-Yeah -- Exact-- That's ge--

00:07:23.276 --> 00:07:25.143
Send me one. That's genius.

00:07:25.143 --> 00:07:26.979
-Nobody wants your sheep.

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.150
[ Both laugh ]

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.452
-Wow. I've never felt more seen.

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.520
-Wow. That is a nerdy thing
that just happened.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:36.655
Alright, I love that.

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.425
-Hey, Jimmy, Jimmy,
that settles it.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.659
-Dude, that settles it.

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:44.096
And by the way,
"a little late to the party,"

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.765
that's a segment
on your show right there.

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:47.199
-Alright, we're gonna
offline this.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:48.434
-"A little late to the party."

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.269
That's what you're doing.
That's a new segment.

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:53.205
Alright. Here we go.

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:55.641
What's your newest mantra?

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:59.378
-My newest mantra
is quite simple.

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.915
It is simply, "What kind of life
do you want to live?"

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:05.083
And I know
that sounds very basic.

00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.319
But the reason
it's been working for me

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:08.287
is I feel like I identified

00:08:08.287 --> 00:08:10.256
so many reasons I used to
get flustered in life

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:11.923
was I'd be
giving away control --

00:08:11.923 --> 00:08:14.459
people online, to producers,
to all this stuff.

00:08:14.459 --> 00:08:15.594
And when you ask yourself,

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:17.930
"What kind of life
do you want to live?"

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.665
it kind of helps you
frame the situation

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.400
where you can take control.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.370
Do you want the life where you
have to listen to these people

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.404
and you have to be
near these people

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.872
and you have to feel this way?

00:08:26.872 --> 00:08:28.641
Or do you want the life where
you can do something about it

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:30.276
and remove yourself
from those situations

00:08:30.276 --> 00:08:32.978
or, like, you know,
take a different path?

00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:34.647
And so, "What kind of life
do you want to live?"

00:08:34.647 --> 00:08:37.483
is a big thing for me.
-I love that.

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.885
There's a new episode of your
show airing tonight on NBC.

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:41.487
Who's on the show tonight?

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:44.189
-Brie Larson! Brie Larson's
on the show, which is --

00:08:44.189 --> 00:08:46.825
I know. I'm like,
"These famouses have taken time

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.127
to talk to me? I'm shook."

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:49.461
-I love Brie Larson.
-But it's super cool.

00:08:49.461 --> 00:08:52.498
She sings and plays me
some of my comments musically.

00:08:52.498 --> 00:08:54.033
So it's super fun.
-No way.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:56.068
-Yeah, I also teach you
how to make a drink.

00:08:56.068 --> 00:09:00.439
A Solo Sex on the Beach,
I teach in my episode today.

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:03.776
Um, and I just want to make it
clear, I'm not a mixologist,

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:06.211
but I do have
a strong will to drink.

00:09:06.211 --> 00:09:08.547
And I believe
it's the same thing.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:10.082
-Congrats on the new season.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:12.151
And you still have
the best fashion,

00:09:12.151 --> 00:09:13.419
best kicks in the game, man.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:15.354
Oh, my God.
Your sneakers, come on.

00:09:15.354 --> 00:09:17.590
Always, always something cool.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.991
New season of
"A Little Late with Lilly Singh"

00:09:19.991 --> 00:09:22.961
airs weeknights at 1:35 on NBC.

00:09:22.961 --> 00:09:24.030
Watch it tonight.

